+  // `+(*a)` compiles to `(?:[^/]*?a)+`, which backtracks exponentially on
+  // inputs like `aaaa!`. When every branch is star-led the repetition is
+  // redundant, so `+(...)` can close like `@(...)` and `*(...)` like `?(...)`
+  // without changing what the pattern matches.
+  if (branches.every(isStarLedBranch)) {
